# SecureVault API - request collection for the VS Code "REST Client"
# extension (humao.rest-client). Click "Send Request" above each block, top
# to bottom. Responses from the login requests are captured by name.
#
# Change the emails before re-running: registering an existing email
# returns 409 by design.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@password = demo-passphrase-123
@alice = alice-http@example.com
@bob = bob-http@example.com

### Health (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### Register alice -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "{{alice}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

### Register alice again -> 409 (duplicate email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "{{alice}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

### Register bob -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "{{bob}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

### Login alice -> 200
# @name aliceLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "{{alice}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

### Login bob -> 200
# @name bobLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "{{bob}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

### Who am I (alice)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Upload sample.pdf as alice -> 201
# @name upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=SecureVaultBoundary

--SecureVaultBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf
--SecureVaultBoundary--

### List alice's documents -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Download -> 200, attachment + nosniff
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/documents/{{upload.response.body.id}}/download
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Bob requests alice's document -> 404 (same as a missing document)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/documents/{{upload.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Bob's list -> 200 []
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{bobLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Text disguised as a PDF -> 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=SecureVaultBoundary

--SecureVaultBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="invoice.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

this is plain text, not a PDF
--SecureVaultBoundary--

### Delete -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/documents/{{upload.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

# 413 (25 MB + 1 byte), quota 409, and 429 need large files or many
# requests - use demo.ps1 for those.
